        "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for lod_lov EA get/generate/parse",
        "message": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for lod_lov EA get/generate/parse\n\nAdd lod_lov_test, covering lod_get_ea(), lod_generate_lovea() and\nlod_parse_striping()/lod_striping_reload(): the LOV EA read/write path\nand the on-disk<->in-core layout conversion that sits around it.\n\nlod_get_ea() is exercised against a mock_ost_obj standing in for\ndt_object_child(dt), covering the xattr-found and -ENODATA cases.\nlod_generate_lovea() and lod_parse_striping()/lod_striping_reload()\nare exercised with every component either LOV_PATTERN_F_RELEASED,\nLOV_PATTERN_MDT, or left un-instantiated (no LCME_FL_INIT): these are\nexactly the cases lod_lov.c itself special-cases to skip real stripe\ndt_object handling, so no OST/OSP object-allocation mock is needed.\n\nEXPORT_SYMBOL() a handful of previously-static-to-the-module lod_lov.c\nhelpers (lod_get_ea, lod_generate_lovea, lod_parse_striping,\nlod_striping_reload, lod_alloc_comp_entries) so the loadable test\nmodule can call them directly.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: AGENT:claude-sonnet-5 [Augment Code]\nChange-Id: I11c6376d1b04d224f5230f69331036522430dc8c\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
